But my calculations were always wrong.

695
00:49:05,992 --> 00:49:07,904
A woman I date shouldn't be calculated.

696
00:49:07,904 --> 00:49:10,740
I think that was the reason why I failed in both of my marriages.

697
00:49:10,740 --> 00:49:14,231
Maybe you didn't like her enough. That's why you were calculating.

698
00:49:14,231 --> 00:49:16,477
If you had really liked her, I don't think you'd have been calculating numbers.

699
00:49:16,477 --> 00:49:19,078
I guess you want to hear I only really like you.

700
00:49:19,524 --> 00:49:20,934
Yes

701
00:49:20,934 --> 00:49:23,305
-I think I liked them all when I married them

702
00:49:23,305 --> 00:49:26,839
-Get out.
-I was about to leave. I have to be somewhere.

703
00:49:26,839 --> 00:49:29,515
-Where do you have to be?
-A welcome party for a divorcee.

704
00:49:32,806 --> 00:49:35,581
"A beast living inside me". You use that quite well.

705
00:49:35,581 --> 00:49:40,587
That's what you said. You should apply for a trademark. The men who cheat for no reason will like that.

706
00:49:40,587 --> 00:49:42,592
I can't give you the custody of child.

707
00:49:43,343 --> 00:49:46,462
If I had wanted you to decide on that matter, I wouldn't have met you in court.

708
00:49:46,901 --> 00:49:49,795
You cannot raise a child with your will and desire only.

709
00:49:49,795 --> 00:49:52,812
I don't think the judge was impressed by you today.

710
00:49:52,913 --> 00:49:55,058
I think we are on equal footing now.

711
00:49:55,058 --> 00:49:59,076
It's too early to celebrate. After the investigation is over, it will move to arbitration.

712
00:50:00,802 --> 00:50:03,530
I really didn't want to hate you this much.

713
00:50:03,530 --> 00:50:07,506
Whenever I see you, every fiber of my being is on the edge.

714
00:50:08,172 --> 00:50:10,536
We had a chance to not become like this.

715
00:50:11,539 --> 00:50:13,226
You threw it away.

716
00:50:13,226 --> 00:50:15,409
You're blaming me? Who asked for the divorce?

717
00:50:15,409 --> 00:50:18,909
Same thing all the time. Why don't you understand that the first one to ask for divorce is the one who's been more patient and tried harder.

718
00:50:22,516 --> 00:50:26,595
You will make me hate even the memories of my loving you.

719
00:50:27,414 --> 00:50:29,528
I wanted to keep them at least.

720
00:51:02,400 --> 00:51:06,093
You're still far away. Far. Seriously.

721
00:51:15,239 --> 00:51:17,782
seriously.

722
00:51:28,302 --> 00:51:30,302
Did you mess it up today as well?

723
00:51:30,302 --> 00:51:34,834
No, not that bad. I will do better next time.

724
00:51:34,834 --> 00:51:40,615
-It shouldn't be "not that bad". You have to do well.
-I know. I will do well next time for sure.

725
00:51:40,615 --> 00:51:45,862
The judge seems to have shifted after learning Dohyun has cheated.

726
00:51:45,862 --> 00:51:49,199
That's a relief. Deulrae is getting married.

727
00:51:49,199 --> 00:51:51,019
with whom? Minho?

728
00:51:52,288 --> 00:51:56,100
They are head over heels for each other. I guess everyone has their soulmate out there.

729
00:51:56,100 --> 00:51:58,850
That's quite a surprise. What does she like about him?

730
00:51:58,850 --> 00:52:01,289
-Because he wants to marry Deulrae he even sold his motorcycle.
-Really?

731
00:52:01,289 --> 00:52:06,435
Deulrae is quite blessed. He owns a building, some land

732
00:52:06,435 --> 00:52:09,887
Even though he's divorced, he doesn't have any kids. He has what he needs to have and doesn't have what's unnecessary.

733
00:52:09,887 --> 00:52:11,788
It's hard for it to be that way.

734
00:52:11,788 --> 00:52:15,509
I am happy to hear a good news in a long time.

735
00:52:15,963 --> 00:52:17,927
-I think it was me.

736
00:52:17,927 --> 00:52:18,834
What was?

737
00:52:18,834 --> 00:52:20,944
The reason Haeyoon broke up

738
00:52:22,218 --> 00:52:24,646
No way. I am sure you're mistaken

739
00:52:24,646 --> 00:52:27,755
No. If I put the pieces together, I think that's the case.

740
00:52:27,755 --> 00:52:30,008
Sangjin said so too.

741
00:52:30,008 --> 00:52:31,805
What if that's really the case?

742
00:52:31,805 --> 00:52:33,078
No way mom.

743
00:52:33,078 --> 00:52:38,113
If I hear that from my daughter, I think my life would be over.

744
00:52:38,113 --> 00:52:41,059
Mom, you're being weak. That's not true.

745
00:52:41,059 --> 00:52:44,184
Even the strong ones, it's different with their children.

746
00:52:44,184 --> 00:52:46,194
You're right. It's not the same with your kids.

747
00:52:46,194 --> 00:52:57,220
I am afraid Taewon will blame me when he grows up or think that I took his dad away from him

748
00:52:57,602 --> 00:53:00,534
This is the reason the parent is always on the losing side to their kids.

749
00:53:00,534 --> 00:53:03,147
Kids make you think all ridiculous notions.

750
00:53:03,147 --> 00:53:08,484
Then why do you have ridiculous thoughts as these? Why do you think you are a hindrance to us?

751
00:53:12,792 --> 00:53:14,641
Shouldn't your name be on the Guinness records?

752
00:53:14,641 --> 00:53:16,283
as the shortest marriage ever?

753
00:53:16,283 --> 00:53:19,651
Britney Spears' marriage lasted 55 hours. He beat her.

754
00:53:19,651 --> 00:53:23,581
-I wasn't counting
-Anyway, congrats on being single again.

755
00:53:23,581 --> 00:53:25,980
I will get divorced soon. All of us are single now then.

756
00:53:25,980 --> 00:53:28,188
-We should party hard one of these day
-Count me out

757
00:53:28,188 --> 00:53:30,725
-With the aunt?
-It turned out that way.

758
00:53:30,725 --> 00:53:35,549
You had to do that. Why get married? Just have fun with her.

759
00:53:35,549 --> 00:53:37,728
Congratulations for not stopping at having fun but getting married

760
00:53:37,728 --> 00:53:39,175
Thank you.

761
00:53:39,175 --> 00:53:40,846
You hold a grudge.

762
00:53:40,846 --> 00:53:43,087
Because I gave you some advice before, you kept that in your mind.

763
00:53:43,087 --> 00:53:44,517
Why are you picking a fight this kid?

764
00:53:44,517 --> 00:53:47,086
I am not a kid. From now on, don't ask me to hang out if Dohyun will be there.

765
00:53:47,699 --> 00:53:50,090
This cute guy. He clearly expresses what he wants.

766
00:53:50,090 --> 00:53:52,923
I don't dislike you. We almost became a family.

767
00:53:52,923 --> 00:53:54,462
I don't have anything against my sister-in-law.

768
00:53:54,462 --> 00:53:57,236
Come to think of it, I almost became a family to you as well Minho.

769
00:53:57,236 --> 00:53:59,757
Please don't drink too much today. I don't want to listen to your drunken tirades.

770
00:54:00,740 --> 00:54:02,803
You're cute. Pour me a glass.

771
00:54:02,803 --> 00:54:04,476
I don't wan to.

772
00:54:04,476 --> 00:54:06,635
I will pour you a glass.

773
00:54:06,635 --> 00:54:10,743
Let's not go home tonight. None of you. We'll stay up here tonight.

774
00:54:10,743 --> 00:54:13,160
-This poor fellow
-What, me?

775
00:54:14,007 --> 00:54:17,323
yes, you. If you want to hold onto Hyejin, just go home.

776
00:54:17,323 --> 00:54:20,716
Don't act out like someone who's seeking attention. Stop it.

777
00:54:20,716 --> 00:54:22,464
I thought you'd know how I would feel.

778
00:54:22,464 --> 00:54:25,621
Looking at how things are panning out, it won't end pleasantly

779
00:54:25,621 --> 00:54:28,115
Let the old farts hang out together and let's step out.

780
00:54:28,115 --> 00:54:30,690
where are you going?

781
00:54:35,232 --> 00:54:37,371
you look well.

782
00:54:38,163 --> 00:54:42,709
I am doing well. Chae Young isn't bad.

783
00:54:43,288 --> 00:54:46,942
I think she's quite something. It would be hard to act like that after being born into that kind of family.

784
00:54:46,942 --> 00:54:51,961
Seeing someone like her, I think nutcases like her change the world for sure.

785
00:55:00,155 --> 00:55:04,198
The favor you asked before. Banking account under an alias. You took your money out because you didn't want to give money to Haejin?

786
00:55:05,546 --> 00:55:08,740
For surgeons, there is a period when you have the golden touch.

787
00:55:08,740 --> 00:55:10,595
I am at my prime now. I know it.

788
00:55:11,303 --> 00:55:14,773
How long do you think I will be able to perform surgery? Do you know how many plastic surgery clinics are there in Gangam alone?

789
00:55:14,773 --> 00:55:19,945
Many more are popping out and in order to survive, I have to continually upgrade my clinic.

790
00:55:19,945 --> 00:55:22,771
Just because things are going well now, there's no guarantee it will all go well later.

791
00:55:22,771 --> 00:55:25,117
I saw many cases when people are ruined with just one mistake.

792
00:55:25,748 --> 00:55:28,031
Asking me to give her half of my assets, that's too much.

793
00:55:28,031 --> 00:55:31,545
I have to survive as well. Haejin doesn't understand how anxious I feel.

794
00:55:31,545 --> 00:55:34,332
I am telling you this because it seems like you don't know what you want.

795
00:55:34,332 --> 00:55:37,159
From what I could see, you seem to want to continue living with Hyejin.

796
00:55:37,159 --> 00:55:40,360
She doesn't want to live with me. She told me fiber of her beings hate me.

797
00:55:40,360 --> 00:55:42,910
Go beg for her forgiveness. In the end, she's bound to give in.

798
00:55:42,910 --> 00:55:46,706
As you continue living with her, fiber of her beings will familiarize themselves to you again.

799
00:55:47,951 --> 00:55:49,926
Do you think it will really work if I beg her?

800
00:55:53,761 --> 00:55:55,816
I guess you don't have to be home tonight.

801
00:55:55,816 --> 00:55:57,965
Do you like me this much?

802
00:56:29,507 --> 00:56:32,956
Mr. Gong Gijoong. It's no fun if you're so easy to predict.

803
00:56:32,956 --> 00:56:34,039
What's so easy to predict?

804
00:56:34,039 --> 00:56:36,561
Why do you come looking for your ex after being divorced?

805
00:56:36,561 --> 00:56:40,071
Are you sure your venture will succeed with such a predictable imagination of yours?

806
00:56:45,646 --> 00:56:47,376
It's cold outside.

807
00:56:47,376 --> 00:56:49,076
I hope it's winter break soon.

808
00:56:49,076 --> 00:56:51,114
-There are not many days left.
-I know.

809
00:56:51,649 --> 00:56:53,522
I haven't washed up. Hurry and wash up first.

810
00:56:53,522 --> 00:56:56,190
-How come you haven't washed up yet?
-I was just laying around

811
00:56:56,190 --> 00:56:57,227
You're here.

812
00:56:57,227 --> 00:57:00,930
Older sis, can you lend me your cleansing cream? I didn't bring anything with me.

813
00:57:00,930 --> 00:57:02,639
Okay.

814
00:57:05,357 --> 00:57:07,093
-Here
-Thank you.

815
00:57:07,914 --> 00:57:10,003
What did you say to Attorney Jung?

816
00:57:10,003 --> 00:57:11,270
What do you mean?

817
00:57:11,270 --> 00:57:17,212
Earlier mom said that Attorney Jung told her that you two broke up because of mom.

818
00:57:17,212 --> 00:57:18,641
I told you to make sure mom wouldn't find out.

819
00:57:18,641 --> 00:57:22,758
You know he's quite smart. I guess that's the conclusion he drew.

820
00:57:22,758 --> 00:57:24,916
Why are you talking as if we're talking about someone else?

821
00:57:24,916 --> 00:57:27,534
Like I told you before, you should have been more careful.

822
00:57:27,534 --> 00:57:29,949
Do I have stop his thoughts?

823
00:57:30,733 --> 00:57:33,788
Even he thinks mom's not being sensible.

824
00:57:34,339 --> 00:57:36,327
you were always like this

825
00:57:36,327 --> 00:57:42,303
when all of us were fighting difficult everyday called life, you built your room and stayed there.

826
00:57:42,303 --> 00:57:50,274
emotional luxury that you enjoy in your room is possible because the mom you criticize fought against the world to make it happen.

827
00:57:51,470 --> 00:57:54,503
Do you know the despair I felt when I gave up on going to college?

828
00:57:56,500 --> 00:57:59,970
I could have gone to college too if I insisted. But I thought of you.

829
00:57:59,970 --> 00:58:03,213
Because if I take a lot, your share decreases.

830
00:58:03,213 --> 00:58:06,813
I thought you were more qualified since you got better grades.

831
00:58:06,813 --> 00:58:10,704
You chose that path. I don't want you to blame me.

832
00:58:10,704 --> 00:58:12,662
I am not blaming you.

833
00:58:12,662 --> 00:58:17,965
When we gave up a little of ours as a family. I am asking what did you give up?

834
00:58:18,405 --> 00:58:21,687
How is it fair that you criticize mom for not being sensible?

835
00:58:21,687 --> 00:58:25,693
Why are you getting worked up over nothing, bringing up past and all?

836
00:58:25,693 --> 00:58:30,633
I am afraid my kid will think like you after I try my best to raise him.

837
00:58:30,633 --> 00:58:33,704
I can you judge your parent under the name of common sense?

838
00:58:33,704 --> 00:58:36,696
If you were going to to do that, you shouldn't have enjoyed the privileges mom gave you.

839
00:58:36,696 --> 00:58:38,993
What kind of privilege did I enjoy?

840
00:58:38,993 --> 00:58:42,778
I worked part time during college and contributed to this household as well.

841
00:58:42,778 --> 00:58:45,335
Working part time for your tuition, is that for the household? That's for yourself.

842
00:58:45,335 --> 00:58:49,471
It's not like you were able to earn full amount of your tuition. You used your pay as your spending money.

843
00:58:49,471 --> 00:58:52,863
What you just said right now, goes against the "common sense" you talk about.

844
00:58:52,863 --> 00:58:57,167
Everyone starts judging parents objectively once they reach puberty.

845
00:58:57,167 --> 00:59:00,174
I am not the odd one out, it's you who stand out.

846
00:59:00,174 --> 00:59:03,131
That's why you were pushed by mom into a wrong marriage.

847
00:59:03,131 --> 00:59:05,786
What? A wrong marriage?

848
00:59:07,700 --> 00:59:11,092
It is a wrong marriage
